pytest is a unit testing framework, it can test a small unit in any program
Advantages : We can group  the testcases, generate reports, we can use dependencies here.

First thing, we have to install Pytest first
--> Go to command prompt --> pip install pytest  (This will install the new version of pytest)

To check if pytest is properly installed or not --> pytest --version
If we get the version, then pytest is installed properly

#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rules:
1. Filename (module) should always start with test_ or end with _test
        Eg : test_filename.py or filename_test.py
2. Classname should always start with Test
        Eg : class TestClassname
3. Function name should always start with test_
        Eg : def test_functionname():

We should follow these conventions because, pytest will automatically recognize the files
starting with test_, automatically recognizes the classes starting with Test,
automatically recognizes the functions starting with test_

To execute --> right click --> open in --> terminal --> pytest test_filename.py

#------------------------------------------------------
-v --> verbocity. This get the detailed explanation
-s --> scripting. This will print all the print statements















